  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "When a positive integer \\(x\\) is divided by a positive integer \\(y,\\) the quotient is \\(u\\) and the remainder is \\(v,\\) where \\(u\\) and \\(v\\) are integers. What is the remainder when \\(x+2uy\\) is divided by \\(y?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2u\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(3u\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(v\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(2v\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The division algorithm gives \\(x=uy+v.\\) Hence \\[x+2uy=3uy+v.\\] The first term is divisible by \\(y,\\) so the remainder is \\(v.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(x=uy+v\\)",
        "Adding a multiple of \\(y\\) does not change the remainder upon division by \\(y\\)"
      ],
